====Usage notes====
{{U:en:who and whom}}

* When {{m|en||who}} (or the other relative pronouns {{m|en|that}} and {{m|en|which}}) is used as the subject of a relative clause, the verb typically agrees with the antecedent of the pronoun. Thus "I who am...", "He who is...", "You who are...", etc.

